EMIT SIDE COMPARISONS BEFORE BINDING THE COMMON RECORD
After contract_version and input_status, complete a_meaning_in_b and b_meaning_in_a.
Within EACH side, emit reviewed_unique_ids and one or two concise factual sentences
of coverage_explanation, then status, THEN only that status's branch-specific fields.
Do not start filling COVERED fields before selecting status; an UNCOVERED result
must not retain harmless_unique_ids or opposite_support_ids from a different branch.

Only after both side comparisons emit anchor_a_ids, anchor_b_ids, a concise
scope_explanation and record_scope. Bind the actual specific record whose facts or
steps you just compared. If a loss describes a particular product, article or result
list, identify what independent core of THAT record the opposite side retains.
Do not switch to their common store, organization, policy or template to manufacture
a shared core for the absent specific record. A retained common FAQ or recruitment
record with an extra step remains a same-record extension under the existing rules.
Shared names/chrome are not sufficient, and ordinary buttons/language differences
are not automatically conflicts. No long debate or repeated restatement is needed.
